ht from violations of locality"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Hossenfelder, S."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/850925"}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1006.2126","label":"41","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"106","artid":"071301","year":2011,"journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett."},"misc":["Taming nonlocality in theories with Planck-scale-deformed Lorentz symmetry"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Amelino-Camelia, G."},{"full_name":"Matassa, M."},{"full_name":"Mercati, F."},{"full_name":"Rosati, G."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/857620"}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1006.2126","label":"42","misc":["Reply to"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Hossenfelder, S."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/857620"}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1006.4587","label":"42","misc":["by Giovanni"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Amelino-Camelia"}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/859226"}}],"number_of_pages":7,"legacy_creation_date":"2012-12-19","preprint_date":"2012-12","author_count":2,"public_notes":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"14 pages"}],"earliest_date":"2012-12","refereed":true,"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"SPIRES","value":"SPIRES-9894462"}],"facet_author_name":["2157025_George Mathew Paily","1015941_Martin Bojowald"],"core":true,"license":[{"imposing":"arXiv","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1208090","updated":"2023-03-07T01:19:37.674319"},"journal_title_variants":["Phys.Rev.D","Phys. Rev. D"],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["gr-qc"],"value":"1212.4773"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["C.Bunster.1","T.Regge.1","D.C.Salisbury.1","J.W.York.1","Jerzy.Lewandowski.1","M.Kagan.3","M.Varadarajan.1","J.Mielczarek.1","M.C.B.Fernandes.2","A.Barrau.1","D.Kovacevic.2","A.Weinstein.2","A.Pachol.1","Daniele.Pranzetti.1","S.Brahma.1","Alejandro.Perez.1","Yaser.Tavakoli.1","S.Meljanac.1","G.M.Paily.1","L.C.Shepley.5","G.M.Hossain.1","J.Kowalski.Glikman.1","Elliot.Nelson.1","T.Thiemann.1","C.Blohmann.1","D.Yamauchi.1","Paul.Adrien.Maurice.Dirac.1","Flavio.Mercati.1","T.Cailleteau.1","S.Shankaranarayanan.1","F.Girelli.1","Y.Sendouda.1","J.David.Brown.1","A.Nowicki.3","Sabine.Hossenfelder.1","J.Grain.1","A.Dapor.1","G.Amelino.Camelia.1","J.Lukierski.1","Giacomo.Rosati.1","K.V.Kuchar.1","S.Hojman.1","A.Starodubtsev.2","J.Magueijo.1","M.Matassa.1","R.Swiderski.1","Martin.Bojowald.1","Lee.Smolin.1","V.N.Tolstoi.1","A.Laddha.1","R.Strajn.1","J.M.Pons.1","A.Henderson.1","N.Deruelle.1","R.Tibrewala.1","J.D.Reyes.1","E.R.Livine.1","M.Sasaki.1","C.Tomlin.1","A.Skirzewski.1","H.Ruegg.1"],"legacy_version":"20170209175347.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology"},{"term":"Theory-HEP"}],"first_author":{"full_name":"Bojowald, Martin","last_name":"Bojowald","first_name":"Martin","recid":1015941},"control_number":1208090,"dois":[{"value":"10.1103/PhysRevD.87.044044"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Bojowald:2012ux"],"abstracts":[{"source":"APS","value":"Deformed special relativity is embedded in deformed general relativity using the methods of canonical relativity and loop quantum gravity. Phase-space dependent deformations of symmetry algebras then appear, which in some regimes can be rewritten as nonlinear Poincaré algebras with momentum-dependent deformations of commutators between boosts and time translations. In contrast to deformed special relativity, the deformations are derived for generators with an unambiguous physical role, following from the relationship between canonical constraints of gravity with stress-energy components. The original deformation does not appear in momentum space and does not give rise to nonlocality issues or problems with macroscopic objects. Contact with deformed special relativity may help to test loop quantum gravity or restrict its quantization ambiguities.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"APS"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"Deformed special relativity is embedded in deformed general relativity using the methods of canonical relativity and loop quantum gravity. Phase-space dependent deformations of symmetry algebras then appear, which in some regimes can be rewritten as non-linear Poincare algebras with momentum-dependent deformations of commutators between boosts and time translations. In contrast to deformed special relativity, the deformations are derived for generators with an unambiguous physical role, following from the relationship between canonical constraints of gravity with stress-energy components. The original deformation does not appear in momentum space and does not give rise to non-locality issues or problems with macroscopic objects. Contact with deformed special relativity may help to test loop quantum gravity or restrict its quantization ambiguities.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"title":"Deformed General Relativity"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Deformed General Relativity"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2013-02-21"}],"curated":true},"updated":"2023-03-07T01:19:37.674319+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1208090?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1208090?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1208090?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1208090?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1208090?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1208090?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1208090"}}],"total":2271},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...role%20of%20general%20relativity...&size=10&page=1","next":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...role%20of%20general%20relativity...&size=10&page=2","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...role%20of%20general%20relativity...&size=10&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...role%20of%20general%20relativity...&size=10&page=1&format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...role%20of%20general%20relativity...&size=10&page=1&format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...role%20of%20general%20relativity...&size=10&page=1&format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...role%20of%20general%20relativity...&size=10&page=1&format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...role%20of%20general%20relativity...&size=10&page=1&format=cv"}}